Z||000008||RedHaze86SD4||12-17-2001||10:33 AM||||Well its probably a typ-o, but alot of mudders and rock crawlers run lower gears in front and highs in back. its so on the road they get better gas mileage, off roading your front pulls more grunt work when ya get in tight spots... just dont go on the road with it or you'll shred the spiders up front. I got my 79 GMC 4x4 for free after the guy drove it 5 miles in 4 wheel on the the highway. there was no front dif left LOL [edit] dang typ-o's  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  and just looked up and yeah theres no way he'd be running the high gears in front. its gotta be the other way around.[edit]<p>[This message has been edited by RedHaze86SD4 (edited 12-17-2001).]||||reg||1
